Nexus Music
===========

Nexus Music is a modified version of SimpMusic.

  Upstream:  SimpMusic, by maxrave-dev and contributors
             https://github.com/maxrave-dev/SimpMusic  (app)
             https://github.com/maxrave-dev/core       (core/ submodule)
  License:   GNU General Public License, version 3 (see LICENSE). Nexus Music is distributed
             under the same license. Its complete corresponding source is this repository
             together with its core/ submodule at the commit recorded here.

All credit for SimpMusic itself — the YouTube Music client, the player, lyrics, analytics,
equalizer, Desktop app and everything else not listed below — belongs to the SimpMusic authors.
Nexus Music is not affiliated with or endorsed by SimpMusic. Please report Nexus-specific problems
to the Nexus maintainer, not to SimpMusic.

Third-party components keep their own licenses and notices; see the in-app open-source licenses
screen (AboutLibraries) and the license headers of the files concerned. In particular,
core/media/media3/src/main/java/androidx/media3/exoplayer/audio/LosslessAudioSink.java is a
modified copy of Media3's DefaultAudioSink (Copyright The Android Open Source Project, Apache-2.0).


Modifications (GPL-3.0 section 5(a): what changed, and when)
-------------------------------------------------------------

2026-11-05  Rebrand to Nexus Music
            App name, launcher icon, applicationId org.nexusmusic.app (.dev for debug),
            Desktop identity (Conveyor names, Windows protocol registration), rootProject name.
            SimpMusic's official-build check is no longer called. Kotlin package names, the
            Android namespace and simpmusic.org services/URLs are unchanged.

2026-11-05  Remove the in-app updater
            Update checks, update dialog, GitHub/F-Droid release lookups, UpdateRepository and
            related settings removed on Android and Desktop.

2026-11-05  Liquid Glass
            Frosted/refractive glass primitives (ui/component/glass/), glass top bars, sheets,
            dialogs, menus and tiles across the app, and a "Liquid Glass" Now Playing style.

2026-11-06  Local music playback
            Play the user's own music files from folders they choose: folder scanning, a Local
            tab in Library, local results in Search, offline playback on Android and Desktop.

2026-11-06  Bit-perfect lossless mode
            Optional bypass of all app DSP for local lossless files, USB bit-perfect mixer
            (Android 14+) and WASAPI exclusive output (Windows), gapless album playback, and an
            audio-quality badge that reports resampling and processing honestly.

2026-11-06  Release and upstream sync
            Nexus version numbering (nexus.properties), release signing script, upstream sync
            script and SYNC.md, upstream CI workflows replaced by a secret-free build check,
            this NOTICE.

2026-11-06  Nexus Violet design
            A dark-purple theme with violet glow as the default colour theme (the old light blue
            stays available as "Classic blue"), a Nexus Violet Now Playing style (spinning circular
            artwork in a glowing ring, neon seek bar and play button), and a Nexus layout for Home
            (greeting header, glowing mood pills, a featured card from the feed).

2026-11-07  Rebranded about and promotion screens
            Upstream's rating, donation, blog and promo pop-ups and links removed from the app;
            the about screen shows Nexus Music text with a GPL-3.0 notice.

2026-11-08  Promotions deleted, India as content country
            The promo dialogs, the remote launch banner and the remote promo line under the
            lyrics are deleted from the source. Content country and charts default to India.
            The debug build is labelled "Nexus Music".

The full history of each change is in the git log of this repository and of core/.
